    },
    {
      "acquisition_source": {
        "advancement_kind": "level_advance",
        "packet_ids": [
          "packet.stage2.011.a8229959146b3e57"
        ],
        "target_cl": 2
      },
      "capabilities": {
        "ai_policy": "BLOCKED_BY_DEPENDENCY",
        "character_sheet": "SUPPORTED",
        "combat_execution": "UNSUPPORTED",
        "gm_display": "NOT_ATTEMPTED"
      },
      "display_name": "Meridian Regulation",
      "display_only_not_execution_authority": true,
      "display_timing_or_category": "Action",
      "full_description": "## CL2 — Meridian Regulation\n\n**Action**  \n**Range:** Touch  \n**Cost:** 1 Qi\n\nChoose one poison, disease, or directly caused physical impairment affecting the target.\n\nThe effect must:\n\n- Have a printed saving throw DC.\n- Not have the Curse, Tribulation, Foundation Injury, Hidden Injury, Possession, Permanent, or Soul Damage tag.\n\n### Effect with Repeat Saves\n\nThe target immediately repeats the saving throw with Advantage.\n\nOn success, apply the effect’s normal successful-save result.\n\n### Effect without Repeat Saves\n\nThe target makes a Constitution saving throw with Advantage against the effect’s printed DC.\n\nOn success, suppress one penalty until the end of the target’s next turn:\n\n- Poisoned.\n- Speed reduction.\n- Disadvantage on attack rolls.\n- Disadvantage on ability checks.\n- Disadvantage on saving throws.\n- Inability to take Reactions.\n\nMeridian Regulation does not automatically:\n\n- Remove the underlying effect.\n- End its duration.\n- Cure the disease or poison.\n- Remove Exhaustion.\n- Restore Hit Points.\n- Stop ongoing damage.\n- Remove a higher-authority effect.\n\n---",
      "full_description_source": "rules_selection_packet",
      "one_line_description": "Spend Qi to help a touched target repeat or suppress a qualifying poison, disease, or physical impairment.",
      "record_hash": "10b9efb4949ceec21f8d209502d644f018376376dc4ad669a43b592e728963c5",
      "record_id": "tianxia.path.qi_cultivation.feature.meridian_regulation",
      "section": "path_features",
      "source": {
        "anchor": "record:tianxia.path.qi_cultivation.feature.meridian_regulation",
