        "combat_execution": "NOT_APPLICABLE",
        "gm_display": "NOT_ATTEMPTED"
      },
      "display_name": "Qi Cultivation Subpath",
      "display_only_not_execution_authority": true,
      "display_timing_or_category": "Feature",
      "full_description": "## Qi Cultivation Subpaths\n\nAt CL3, choose one Qi Cultivation Subpath for which you have legal access. You gain its features at CL3, CL6, CL10, CL14, and CL18.\n\n| Catalog classification | Meaning |\n|---|---|\n| **Open School** | Commonly teachable or institutionally available. Open access does not imply low power. |\n| **Restricted Scripture** | Controlled technical, political, military, medical, inherited, or hazardous instruction. |\n| **Rare Inheritance** | Uncommon structural access, bloodline, vessel, destiny, treasure, or singular transmission. A **Rare Variant** is a parent-lineage conversion inside this category. |\n| **Forbidden Variant** | A parent-lineage conversion carrying a prohibited, condemned, hazardous, predatory, or politically unacceptable price. Forbidden is not automatically Daemonic. |\n| **Secret Law** | Qualitatively superior law-level authority requiring explicit access and its printed initiation price. |\n| **Daemonic** | A mechanical tag used only when the Source Rule interacts with Corruption, daemonic energy, purification, or anti-daemonic rules. It is orthogonal to social accusations of being “demonic.” |\n\nA character normally has one Subpath progression. Parent and Variant lineages use the executable replacement rules in Shared Qi Subpath Rules R4; they do not provide a second simultaneous Subpath progression.\n\n---",
      "full_description_source": "rules_selection_packet",
      "one_line_description": "Choose a legal Qi Cultivation Subpath at CL3 and gain its progression features.",
      "record_hash": "4ebfb354f40ba525d1eb8914605878893437c2fab6d7db8abb2c5d194276f818",
      "record_id": "tianxia.path.qi_cultivation.feature.qi_cultivation_subpath",
