      "display_name": "Qi Sensing",
      "display_only_not_execution_authority": true,
      "display_timing_or_category": "Feature",
      "full_description": "## CL1 — Qi Sensing\n\nQi Sensing is always active unless suppressed.\n\n### Passive Sensing\n\nWithin 30 feet, perceive the presence of active supernatural energy from:\n\n- Path and Subpath features.\n- Sphere talents.\n- Formations.\n- Talismans.\n- Cultivated items.\n- Active spirits.\n- Concentrated Cultivation Points.\n- Transformations.\n- Active curses.\n- Active seals.\n- Possession.\n- Corruption.\n- Strong residues created during the previous hour.\n\nQi Sensing is blocked by:\n\n- 1 foot of stone.\n- 1 inch of common metal.\n- A thin sheet of lead.\n- 3 feet of wood or packed earth.\n- A sealed Formation or effect explicitly blocking Qi perception.\n\nPassive Qi Sensing does not automatically reveal:\n\n- The exact technique.\n- Exact statistics.\n- A precise occupied space for an Invisible creature.\n- A dormant inheritance.\n- A secret property.\n- A successful concealment effect.\n\n### Analyze Qi\n\n**Action**  \n**Range:** 30 feet\n\nChoose one detected effect, creature, item, or residue.\n\nLearn:\n\n- Its broad category.\n- Its active supernatural tags.\n- Whether its Source CL is lower than, equal to, or higher than yours.\n- Whether it is active, dormant, damaged, unstable, or suppressed.\n\nFor a concealed effect, make a Cultivation Check against its save DC.\n\nIf it has no save DC, use:\n\n`8 + source Proficiency Bonus + source key ability modifier`\n\nOn failure:\n\n- You know concealed power is present.\n- You do not learn its exact nature or location.\n- You cannot retry until the effect changes or a new scene begins.\n\nWhen the check succeeds, the AI GM must provide the listed information and cannot withhold it for dramatic convenience.\n\n---",
      "full_description_source": "rules_selection_packet",
      "one_line_description": "Passively sense active supernatural energy nearby and analyze one detected source in detail.",
      "record_hash": "0b40cc6412f3ce3e68d042c97d502474db3aa10525c219b6038eb567930a30dd",
      "record_id": "tianxia.path.qi_cultivation.feature.qi_sensing",
